Object class is the parent class of all classes in java.
Throwable is the class which is the parent of Error and Exception class

Object
   |
   └── Throwable (The Root of all "Catchables")
        |
        ├── Error (System-level/Fatal - Do NOT catch)
        |    ├── VirtualMachineError
        |    |    ├── OutOfMemoryError
        |    |    └── StackOverflowError
        |    ├── LinkageError
        |    |    └── NoClassDefFoundError
        |    ├── ThreadDeath
        |    └── IOError (Severe physical I/O failure)
        |
        └── Exception (Application-level - OK to catch)
             |
             ├── RuntimeException (Unchecked - Logic errors)
             |    ├── ArithmeticException
             |    ├── NullPointerException
             |    ├── ArrayIndexOutOfBoundsException
             |    └── IllegalArgumentException
             |
             ├── IOException (Checked - External issues)
             |    ├── FileNotFoundException
             |    └── EOFException
             |
             ├── SQLException (Checked - Database issues)
             |
             └── ClassNotFoundException (Checked)
             
In the above Exceptions, all the exception are Checked Exceptions, meaning compiler won't force us to handle those exceptions.
And the SQLException,IOException are checked expression because compiler will force us to handle that type of exceptions.
